# Shell scripts and generated JS/Python must stay LF even on Windows checkouts.
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite these to
# CRLF; bash then fails on every line with `$'\r': command not found` (and a
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` shebang gives "bad interpreter"). Scoped to text types
# on purpose — a blanket `* text=auto` would corrupt binary assets under
# plugins/*/assets/.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
# Extensionless shell hooks — a CRLF checkout makes bash die at `set -euo
# pipefail\r` on the first line, breaking the Windows commit path.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
# Markdown must stay LF too. `ml-toolkit:cv-explorer` was the only skill stored
# with CRLF (SKILL.md + 5 references), so nothing normalized it and no guard saw
# it: every runtime parsed the frontmatter, but any shell lifted out of those
# fences carried a trailing \r. Scoped to *.md rather than widened to `* text=auto`
# for the same reason as above — a blanket rule would corrupt binary assets.
*.md   text eol=lf
